From 85189f3b427338f77a41fb38eff528b946ecd758 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 02:53:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(entities): apply native fishing bite impulses

Apply ViaBedrock's bite message to the current fishing hook on the client
thread. Require the active connection and the exact Java spawn UUID so
queued messages cannot affect a replaced hook, another entity, or another
connection. Preserve horizontal motion and delegate float vertical addition
to the core calculation verified against the pinned native executable.

Bedrock event 13 adds -0.5 to existing vertical motion. Java has no standard
additive-motion update for a tracked hook. A dedicated capability works for
both direct translation and ViaProxy without guessing an authoritative
velocity or enabling Java's unrelated biting timer. Core also translates splash sound and the ordinary Java wake fallback.
Later hook physics and complete visible parity remain separate work.

Play the native hook effect and both distinct wake emissions using the
current local position, collision-box minimum and width. Keep the surface
floor and unnormalized direction calculation in core. Native legacy
WaterWake forwards to the named water-wake graph; retain its second
emission instead of deduplicating it. Each emitter has independent Molang
state and a fixed world origin, so reeling does not move existing effects.
Use Java fishing particles when a licensed wake graph is unavailable.
The wire format and spawn/connection guards remain unchanged.

Prepare resources and independent Molang environments off the render thread.
The cold archive load otherwise delayed live rod input by about 850 ms.
Bound pending preparation to 32 requests and reject stale resource generations
and worlds before starting effects. Keep the bite impulse immediate.

Apply the legacy wake distance gate using the rendered camera, raw chunk
setting and a persisted continuous native particle-distance slider. Keep
the two named emissions independent and sample the decision before async
preparation. Core owns the calculation and native option semantics; only
local camera sampling and settings presentation require this integration.
The pinned option starts at zero and ignores changes within 0.001, without
quantizing values. Use the native Minecraft slider with keyboard controls.
